\section{Introduction}

Einstein, Podolsky and Rosen questioned whether quantum mechanics is complete \cite{einstein1935can}. Bell showed that local hidden-variable theories obey inequalities that quantum mechanics violates \cite{bell1964einstein}, and early experiments with time-varying analyzers confirmed the violation \cite{aspect1982experimental}.

\section{Theory}

For analyzer settings $a, a'$ and $b, b'$ the CHSH combination of correlations is

\begin{equation}
  \label{eq:chsh}
  S = E(a, b) - E(a, b') + E(a', b) + E(a', b')
\end{equation}

Local hidden-variable models satisfy $|S| \le 2$, while quantum mechanics allows $|S| = 2\sqrt{2}$ at optimal settings; see Eq.~\eqref{eq:chsh}.

